   background-color: @@colour;\n    }\n    .createButtonColours( @colour-array, @n, @i + 1 )\n}\n\n.button{\n    font-weight: 600;\n    color: #f5f5f5;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    margin: .25em;\n    padding: .5em 1em;\n    transition: background-color .2s ease-in-out;\n    .createButtonColour(#666);\n    .createButtonColours();\n}\n```\n\nShould output:\n\n``` less\n.button {\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: #f5f5f5;\n  border-radius: 3px;\n  margin: .25em;\n  padding: .5em 1em;\n  transition: background-color 0.2s ease-in-out;\n  background-color: #666;\n  border: 1px solid #535353;\n}\n.button:hover,\n.button:active,\n.button:target,\n.button:focus {\n  background-color: #595959;\n}\n.button.red {\n  background-color: #E74C3C;\n}\n.button.red-2 {\n  background-color: #C0392B;\n}\n.button.orange {\n  background-color: #F39C12;\n}\n.button.orange-2 {\n  background-color: #E67E22;\n}\n.button.orange-3 {\n  background-color: #D35400;\n}\n.button.yellow {\n  background-color: #F1C40F;\n}\n.button.green {\n  background-color: #2ECC71;\n}\n.button.green-2 {\n  background-color: #27AE60;\n}\n.button.turquoise {\n  background-color: #1ABC9C;\n}\n.button.turquoise-2 {\n  background-color: #16A085;\n}\n.button.blue {\n  background-color: #3498DB;\n}\n.button.blue-2 {\n  background-color: #2980B9;\n}\n.button.purple {\n  background-color: #9B59B6;\n}\n.button.purple-2 {\n  background-color: #8E44AD;\n}\n.button.navy {\n  background-color: #34495E;\n}\n.button.navy-2 {\n  background-color: #2C3E50;\n}\n.button.grey {\n  background-color: #ECF0F1;\n}\n.button.grey-2 {\n  background-color: #BDC3C7;\n}\n.button.grey-3 {\n  background-color: #95A5A6;\n}\n.button.grey-4 {\n  background-color: #7F8C8D;\n}\n```\n\nLike it does on this [less2css.org example](http://goo.gl/VkG1rk)\n\nExcept gulp-less (v. 3.0.5) gives me the error `variable @undefined is undefined` on the line where `@@colour` is mentioned. Now - forgetting this other issue - if I remove this and replace it with a `wid